Z||000004||AusFiero||08-11-2001||08:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by overlord:<BR><B>just noticed the steering wheel..  Did it come like that from the factory or whats the deal?   dont shun me if it is a dum question but i sereioulsy dont know...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>sharp ride btw......cant wait for after pics.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks Overlord. I do my best to keep it nice.<P>As for the RHD, no it isn't a factory job, it is a local conversion. Average cost to convert a Fiero to RHD is about AU$5000 or cheaper if you do it yourself. I bought mine already converted but have practically redone it all due to bad workmanship by the original convertor. We can now drive any car over 16 years (I think it is 16) old without converting them. <P>HMMMM but whats wrong with "converting" a 16 year old I suppose  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
